    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50902" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἶρος</span></b> , ὁ,
		<u>Irus</u>, a name given by the suitors to the Ithacan beggar
		Arnaeus because he carried messages (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἶρις</span>), <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			18.5
		</span></i> sq.: hence, later as Appellat., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>an Irus</i>, i.e. <i>a beggar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				18.140
			</span></i>: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἶροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Nav.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			.</div>
